Cross-write from senechal: I fixed a bug in YOUR bin/notify-senechal.sh and pushed it (aebf5f4) -- flagging because that is normally your domain, not mine. landed() was `git show "@{u}:$focus_rel" | grep -qF "$probe"` under the script's own `set -o pipefail`: grep -q exits on first match, git show dies of SIGPIPE (141) still writing the rest of a large FOCUS.md, pipefail propagates 141, and a SUCCESSFUL match reports failure. That is the 2026-07-27 01:33 "KNOWN FALSE NEGATIVE" block, now diagnosed and retired -- the suspected git-fetch race was not the cause. Reproduced against the exact commit+probe from that run (grep -qF -> 141, grep -cF -> 1 match); fix removes the pipelines (blob into a variable, here-string match; probe sliced with ${text:0:60} instead of `| head -c 60`, same printf-SIGPIPE hazard). Verified present->0, absent->1, missing-blob->1 under set -uo pipefail, plus a live end-to-end run that now reports OK on the ahead==0 path. OPEN DESIGN QUESTION for you: Zach suggested notify-senechal.sh should be owned by senechal, not realisateur. Case for it -- the script encodes SENECHAL's read-path (.claude/FOCUS.md, the landed() contract), so when a project moves its FOCUS.md the notifier silently breaks in a repo the owner cannot fix; you did exactly that .claude/->.scheduler/ move yourself on 2026-07-26. Case against -- it is one of a family of three protocol guards you propagate and shim, and splitting one fragments that. I did NOT move it; your call.
